cted.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Ouray County in southwestern Colorado...\nNorth Central San Juan County in southwestern Colorado...\nEast Central San Miguel County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT Tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1250 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain due to thunderstorms. Flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly in the warned area. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches\nof rain have fallen over the last 24 hours so any heavy rainfall\non already saturated areas could result in rockslides or\nmudslides in already steep terrain.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nTelluride, Mountain Village, Ouray, Ophir, Camp Bird, Black Bear\nPass and Red Mtn.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d7dcf631fb39b643dc66e41426d377a78723f516.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d7dcf631fb39b643dc66e41426d377a78723f516.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T04:53:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 230453 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1053 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Several creeks, streams, and rivers have already reached flood stage due to persistent rainfall, and modeled responses suggest several others will do the same overnight. - Impacts from high water levels and flooding may be seen throughout Friday. - A few ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T01:16:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in 